      "DAISY: They're -- fascinating.\nMISSY: Excuse me, I should have knocked.",
      "ELEANOR: Who’d like coffee? Your Mother has now told me for the tenth time -- not to call her Royal Highness -- Elizabeth.\nMISSY: She’s told me that too. Daisy? Daisy? Hello? Anyone home in there?\nDAISY: What?? Oh yes. She told me that too.\nELEANOR: I told her who did she think I was?",
      "MISSY: Daisy’s blushing again.\nELEANOR: What is she thinking? What’s going on in that mind?",
      "MISSY: \"A large part of the country still believes that Edward, Duke of Windsor, is the rightful owner of the British throne --\nELEANOR: “Thrones?’ ‘Kings and Dukes.’ It all sounds like the Middle Ages.",
      "ELIZABETH: Charming.\nELEANOR: Hopefully not too small.\nELIZABETH: Look at that view. You must tell me about everything.\nELEANOR: That's -- the field."
    ]
